 intriguing of the Raiders' 27 free agents","description":"A former No. 4 overall pick, a Pro Bowl linebacker and their starting quarterback the final two games are among the Raiders who will hit the market.","published":"2023-03-04T00:42:03.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/las-vegas-raiders/post/_/id/27320/looking-at-the-most-intriguing-of-the-raiders-28-free-agents","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Paul Gutierrez","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Revamped Las Vegas Raiders cornerback room wants to show 'dawg mentality'","description":"The Raiders have two new outside cornerbacks, who will get tested early and often in an AFC West that's loaded with star quarterbacks.","published":"2022-09-09T00:02:00.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/las-vegas-raiders/post/_/id/27001/revamped-las-vegas-raiders-cornerback-room-wants-to-show-dawg-mentality","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Paul Gutierrez","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Rock Ya-Sin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Ya-Sin","description":"American football player (born 1996)","touched":"2026-11-26T23:15:18Z","intro":"Abdurrahman \"Rock\" ibn Ramadan Ya-Sin (born May 23, 1996) is an American professional football cornerback for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Presbyterian Blue Hose, before transferring to the Temple Owls. He was selected by the Indianapolis Colts in the second round of the 2019 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Ya-Sin attended Southwest DeKalb High School in Decatur, Georgia. He was ranked as a two-star recruit and committed to Presbyterian on February 5, 2015."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"After Presbyterian decided to move to a non-scholarship conference in the Football Championship Subdivision, Ya-Sin transferred mid-year to Temple. After recording 44 tackles, two tackles-for-loss, two interceptions, and 12 pass breakups, Ya-Sin was selected to play in the 2019 Senior Bowl."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"INDIANAPOLIS COLTS\n\n2019 SEASON\nYa-Sin was drafted by the Indianapolis Colts in the second round with the 34th overall pick in the 2019 NFL draft. In Week 11 against the Jacksonville Jaguars, Ya-Sin recorded his first career interception off a pass thrown by Nick Foles in the 33–13 win. Ya-Sin was named to Pro Football Focus' All-Rookie Team.\n\n2020 SEASON\nYa-Sin switched his jersey number to 26 before the season, stating he wanted \"a new beginning\". He was inactive against the Minnesota Vikings in week 2 due to a stomach illness.\nIn Week 11 against the Green Bay Packers, Ya-Sin recorded his first interception of the season off a pass thrown by Aaron Rodgers during the 34–31 overtime win.\n\nLAS VEGAS RAIDERS\nOn March 16, 2022, Ya-Sin was traded to the Las Vegas Raiders in exchange for Yannick Ngakoue. He played in 11 games with nine starts, recording 45 tackles and seven passes defensed.\n\nBALTIMORE RAVENS\nOn May 3, 2023, Ya-Sin signed a one-year, $6 million contract with the Baltimore Ravens. Ya-Sin made 14 appearances (including one start) for the Ravens, recording two pass deflections and 13 combined tackles.\n\nSAN FRANCISCO 49ERS\nOn April 11, 2024, Ya-Sin signed a one-year contract with the San Francisco 49ers. Ya-Sin made 13 appearances for San Francisco, compiling two pass deflections and three combined tackles.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn March 20, 2025, Ya-Sin signed with the Detroit Lions. He played in all 17 games with six starts as the Lions third cornerback, recording 47 tackles and nine passes defensed.\nOn March 16, 2026, Ya-Sin re-signed with the Lions on a one-year, $4 million contract."}],"wikidataId":"Q61746860","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-03-16","text":"Signed DB Roger McCreary, LB Malcolm Rodriguez and DB Rock Ya-Sin."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3910229","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/Y/Ya-SRo00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/rock-ya-sin/49564","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/rock-ya-sin/7825","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Ya-Sin"},"insights":["Ranks 1st of 112 qualified cornerbacks in missed-tackle %.","Ranks 16th of 112 qualified cornerbacks in yards allowed per target.","On the field for 52% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $3.2M is the 18th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}